*.sh text eol=lf
installer/tests/*.sh text eol=lf
src/Huddle.App/AvatarLibrary/*.png binary
# Shipped byte-for-byte in every release archive, and the installer skips npm ci only while the
# lock file's SHA-256 is unchanged. Without a fixed EOL a Windows checkout gets CRLF, so a release
# built there differs from the Linux-built one and every upgrade reruns npm ci (release smoke STEP 7).
tools/acp/package.json text eol=lf
tools/acp/package-lock.json text eol=lf
